OL,3,APalace in war of words with Earl
OL,4,ASpencer over claims in Diana book
OL,5,
OL,6,FBuckingham Palace is in a war of words
OL,7,Fwith Earl Spencer, the brother of
OL,8,FDiana, Princess of Wales, over a
OL,9,Fcontroversial memoir about her life and
OL,10,Fdeath.
OL,12,FKing Charles is accused of
OL,13,Finsensitively saying to Earl Spencer,
OL,14,Fin the wake of Diana's death in 1997,
OL,15,Fthat "we'll forget her soon enough",
OL,16,Faccording to excerpts published in the
OL,17,FDaily Mail.
OL,19,FBut the Palace has pushed back
OL,20,Funusually strongly, angered by the
OL,21,Fclaims and attempting to cast doubt on
OL,22,Fthem.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/20
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1789647589
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,APalace in war of words with Earl
OL,4,ASpencer over claims in Diana book
OL,5,
OL,6,F"While we do not comment on books as a
OL,7,Fmatter of principle, His Majesty is
OL,8,Fmindful that the pain of fraternal
OL,9,Fgrief can cloud reason, affect judgment
OL,10,Fand colour memory in ways others do not
OL,11,Frecognise, even many years after such a
OL,12,Floss," it said.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/20
